<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:25:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>King Charles says he has greater understanding of 'horrors' of slavery, falls short of apology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9aa2f5155a307728089fb524e06d8dabc6a57c6dd1b46857e3eba95610abd23</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology--ae418e66f435.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology" /><summary type="html">King Charles III told the heads of 56 Commonwealth countries on Tuesday that he has a greater understanding of the horrors of slavery, calling it a "shameful chapter of history". This comes as Prime Minister Andy Burnham said he was open to the United Kingdom apologising for the transatlantic slave trade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland foils attempted 'provocation' on Russian border, PM Tusk says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02fe3134c764db5857cfcdece0f4b9a3ee3d59f9b7c6441025ea5b7456488b</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:39:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says--aab9903dd48c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Donald Tusk said Tuesday that Poland prevented an attempted "provocation" on its border with the Russian exclave of Kaliningrad overnight. He gave few details but said Polish security forces prevented any incident from happening.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French schools blockade resume on smaller scale as holidays end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91ee18b837b0b90e12e256137984e6b5d47b1d0fd2134b1135dc57fa66f1fd20</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:01:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end--e0c3a170632d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end" /><summary type="html">Students blockaded dozens of high schools across France on Tuesday to maintain pressure on the government over education reforms as trade unions prepared for a nationwide strike later this week. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cheese theft becomes rife among Europe's gangsters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60f2308bb9ad07b41b246d4434c977906201a664df555016a10525de7112f831</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:25:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:53:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261103-cheese-theft-becomes-rife-among-europe-s-gangsters--0e5372666128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261103-cheese-theft-becomes-rife-among-europe-s-gangsters" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, November 3: We look at reactions and analyses in Poland, where pro-European Prime Minister Donald Tusk is involved in a standoff with the nationalist president over the composition of the constitutional court. In other news, there's fresh outrage at big tech, after Google went rogue in Finland and cut down 250,000 trees for data centre projects. Finally, cheese is France's most stolen food product, and it's the stuff of cold, calculated crime.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>European force to hold first Ukraine support exercise in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:184196029fc210e651b89fc405a9b11f7b5424bcefc50226d0d926bb41b2f3a1</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-european-force-to-hold-first-ukraine-support-exercise-in-poland--f3232a2d9c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-european-force-to-hold-first-ukraine-support-exercise-in-poland" /><summary type="html">Around 2,800 troops from 10 European countries will take part in a military exercise in southeastern Poland from November 9 to 22, testing a multinational force designed to support Ukraine after a potential ceasefire. Led by France and Britain, the force aims to bolster Ukraine's security without taking on an offensive role.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe's Gen Z protesters unite over living costs, housing and employment uncertainty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec014e2ab5b3c095faefd17468860cf5e184f1d4c04941b78c17c2c469c6412a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:25:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:21:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-europe-s-gen-z-protesters-unite-over-living-costs-housing-and-uncertainty-of-getting-jobs--7a88fa7032d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-europe-s-gen-z-protesters-unite-over-living-costs-housing-and-uncertainty-of-getting-jobs" /><summary type="html">Although French high schoolers may have taken the lead in the youth protests that have since spread to Belgium, Germany, Italy, Portugal and Spain, they acted like "a catalyst" for their shared concerns over their future, researchers say, pointing to higher living costs, unaffordable housing and the uncertainty of their employment prospects.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes kill at least 26 in Ukraine after war's longest ceasefire ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd33b3947aca0a8d9e3ec5a751be89d38ee1db141115dbfa8793f408422ae0d3</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:18:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-russian-strikes-kill-26-in-ukraine-after-longest-ceasefire-ends--a4e958250ed1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-russian-strikes-kill-26-in-ukraine-after-longest-ceasefire-ends" /><summary type="html">Russia killed at least 26 people in strikes on a village in southern Ukraine on Monday, including civilians collecting humanitarian aid, emergency workers and police officers. The attack came hours after a rare ceasefire ended, extinguishing hopes of progress towards peace.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b4f149611806ee7e8b0f00b639fe42c43e9a258a9e04949716102198dd6acfa</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T22:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261102-emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says--3e24a09abf48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261102-emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyberattacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kinds of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e6b4355a799635d9f46b5628bbfd52e6cd7609e848d804f4ae5676ad6c0cef9</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T22:28:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says--2d0c015e47b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyberattacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kinds of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".</summary></entry><entry><title>The Long Hull: Karl Bushby reflects on perseverance &amp; 'best of humanity' on his 28-year journey home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66df82e895e19e418cc3f8b8aab4e3616564e282545c6307ff75276d9b933d4a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T20:54:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261102-the-long-hull-karl-bushby-reflects-on-perseverance-best-of-humanity-on-his-28-year-journey---36a7e13bd371.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261102-the-long-hull-karl-bushby-reflects-on-perseverance-best-of-humanity-on-his-28-year-journey-home" /><summary type="html">"They say it takes a village. In this case, it took a world." After 28 years and some 50,000 kilometres, British explorer and adventurer Karl Bushby has returned to his hometown of Hull, completing an extraordinary life journey across four continents that illustrates not only the limits of human endurance, but also the intricate relationship between individual determination, geopolitical constraints and a world of humanity.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>EU says fridge attacks 'deliberate attempt to disrupt' bloc's food supply</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce63375459672180ddc3686688b04d6e6c85766dea46fb962c73584015cc762e</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T20:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-fridge-attacks-deliberate-attempt-to-disrupt-bloc-s-food-supply--66c4d792c545.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-fridge-attacks-deliberate-attempt-to-disrupt-bloc-s-food-supply" /><summary type="html">Grocery stores from Sweden to Portugal were hit Monday by a suspected cyberattack on their freezer systems, in what the EU denounced as a deliberate attempt to disrupt the bloc's food chain. Supermarkets in Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg and the Netherlands were among at least eight countries affected in the incident, which came three weeks after a cyberattack caused mass disruption in French grocery stores. Food retailers were forced to throw out produce that had spoiled or was at risk of spoiling after refrigerator temperatures soared overnight. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia again pummels Ukraine after rare pause in fighting in Kherson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc46a3a7da34a245e4895b7572b27724014af23936b969ebb7f4536a48dc1b4a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T18:53:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-russia-pummels-ukraine-again-after-rare-pause-in-fighting-in-kherson--2e4e1b64c914.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-russia-pummels-ukraine-again-after-rare-pause-in-fighting-in-kherson" /><summary type="html">Intense fighting between Russia and Ukraine again picked up after a rare ceasefire allowed for a humanitarian mission to reach the war-torn, Russian-occupied city of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region. While Russia accused Kyiv of sending hundreds of drones toward Moscow overnight into Tuesday, Kyiv said Russia had killed dozens of civilians lining up for aid in Zaporizhzhia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Refrigeration cyberattacks highlight risks of connecting industry to the internet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cde8f68eb9fd4ba045069302719fdc1aceade3911f09345a0b56059c8ec88a7e</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-caught-cold-fridge-cyberattack-highlights-internet-gadget-weaknesses--721c22a98b74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-caught-cold-fridge-cyberattack-highlights-internet-gadget-weaknesses" /><summary type="html">Cyberattacks affecting supermarket refrigeration systems on Monday in several European countries – including Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg, the Netherlands and Sweden – have highlighted the risks of connecting industrial infrastructure to the internet.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>British adventurer arrives back at mother's home after 28-year journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:980f0c5fcc205f04ea21113f00b201347efd90f21f6b0dae48bc8b7d9e1f068c</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:45:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey--f46b5480775f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey" /><summary type="html">British adventurer Karl Bushby enjoyed an emotional reunion with his mother and family on Monday, as he arrived back home after a 28-year, 50,000-kilometre trek from South America, crossing four continents on foot.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia report fake emergency alerts after cyberattacks target apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12377ae182adb14f3b73aabcd67e5142804963230adec08ef5c8f53de3fbd616</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:06:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps--d0b256d1a838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Ukraine and Russia said their emergency alert mobile apps had been targeted by cyberattacks, with users in Ukraine receiving false warnings of an imminent nuclear threat. Moscow said that hackers had sent fake emergency alerts after gaining access to the Russian Emergency Situations Ministry’s mobile app, and that efforts were ongoing to restore the app's functionality.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fresh wave of fridge cyberattacks hits European supermarkets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eb2e88b5be5085ffe7a9b80198b0050319e270c4c5799926305e89b03208643</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets--81a7e18ccf01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets" /><summary type="html">Stores and supermarkets across Belgium, Luxembourg, Finland, Estonia and Sweden all reported early Monday abrupt temperature spikes in their fridges and freezers in an apparent cyberattack targeting refrigeration units. The incidents follow a similar attack that hit hundreds of supermarkets across France in October, triggering food loss and fires.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italian journalists under police protection as threats rise across the country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3f3e403e8a71ffd4af4f8ae2e08c691223e231e32a0ab0e059df7a355a12ab3</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:20:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country--830ee8076ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country" /><summary type="html">Italy is the European country with the largest number of journalists under police protection. There, journalism is a profession particularly susceptible to threats and intimidation, but the European Union's measures to protect press freedom are slow to be implemented. FRANCE 24's team has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Consolidation of power': Bulgaria elects Iliana Iotova as first woman president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:210be5e2166398b93bbb289eb6bb3f36a15244985ee53120e7d5acdaba7b0240</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261102-consolidation-of-power-bulgaria-elects-iliana-iotova-as-first-woman-president--8be991b44926.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261102-consolidation-of-power-bulgaria-elects-iliana-iotova-as-first-woman-president" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, November 2: Bulgarian papers discuss the country's new president. In Belarus, some political prisoners are held in psychiatric wards instead of prisons. Also: Hitler's Eagle's Nest burned down. Will it be rebuilt and should it? Finally, the queen of Halloween, Heidi Klum, flaunts her most disgusting costume yet.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Former UK paratrooper Karl Bushby ends 28-year trek across jungles and frozen sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:621d8d214b7db18c10b0ca4473cda0bae99584185524aa3d227a7d1511ea3bf5</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T10:13:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-former-uk-paratrooper-karl-bushby-ends-28-year-trek-across-jungles-and-frozen-sea--6b241b23dc52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-former-uk-paratrooper-karl-bushby-ends-28-year-trek-across-jungles-and-frozen-sea" /><summary type="html">Former British paratrooper Karl Bushby on Monday came to the end of his 28-year trek around the world, arriving in his native city of Hull after having swum across the English Channel. His journey took him from the southern tip of Latin America up across the frozen Bering Strait before crossing through Central Asia and Europe to return home.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France: Some schools blocked as limited youth protests resume after holidays</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a38f6e6c40d6356e25f2ba812d3c9f4fa1d01f7e762f87035cf788c40b9a5d8</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T09:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-france-some-schools-blocked-as-limited-youth-protests-resume-after-holidays--e8fe347b0113.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-france-some-schools-blocked-as-limited-youth-protests-resume-after-holidays" /><summary type="html">French students returning from autumn holidays blocked some high schools on Monday, November 2, determined to reinvigorate a protest movement despite government concessions during the break. FRANCE 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>RSF publishes list of press freedom 'predators': 'Dictators want to silence journalists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ede2d1ba563f97f1fa024d5b3c13d6e5bf501a9252939f507c84d33d09f5f17</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T09:06:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rsf-publishes-list-of-press-freedom-predators-dictators-want-to-silence-journalists--8b5f1d5c3a8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rsf-publishes-list-of-press-freedom-predators-dictators-want-to-silence-journalists" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Thibaut Bruttin, Director General and Secretary-General of Reporters Without Borders (RSF), who says, “When a journalist is killed, it is everyone's right to know what is being endangered.” His warning captures the central democratic dilemma explored in this interview marking the United Nations' International Day to End Impunity for Crimes Against Journalists. As journalists confront lethal violence, imprisonment, political intimidation and increasingly hostile working environments, the struggle for press freedom has become inseparable from a more fundamental question: who controls the public's access to truth? For RSF, press freedom is not simply a journalist's right to speak, but society's right to know.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia bombing kills at least 26 people at aid centre in Ukraine's Zaporizhzhia region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39ee6dadebf367b423b28df0cacc8a50111853beb667aa2fb29ab0c8bc3c36b7</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T06:19:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends--a26586664aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends" /><summary type="html">Russian forces on Monday bombed ‌a village in Ukraine's southeastern Zaporizhzhia region, killing at least 26 people including two rescue workers, Ukrainian authorities said. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky alleged that ‌Russian forces repeatedly dropped aerial bombs ‌on a school in the village of Komyshuvakha that was being used to distribute humanitarian assistance. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine accuse each other of hacking emergency alert apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4019a14ea52a0dd2cec777cf23a5811c6f09463467dda37c4f34054837991f1</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T01:20:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked--083a045e3724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine accused each other of hacking their emergency alert applications after a local ceasefire in the war's eastern Kherson region expired on Sunday. The cyberattacks came as both sides warned of renewed fighting and Kyiv signalled it could halt strikes on Russian oil refineries in exchange for US Patriot missiles.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland rocked by Constitutional showdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63266d2b9b90c230c82572683cf895fd9f82ba1591a90dde4d8026a1e5c66caf</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown--f25dbb628a78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown" /><summary type="html">Poland’s constitutional crisis deepened on Saturday as the European Commission urged President Karol Nawrocki to recognise new judges appointed by Prime Minister Donald Tusk. The standoff comes ahead of next year’s parliamentary election, with polls suggesting a close race between Tusk’s coalition and the nationalist right. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region ends after Russia refuses extension</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de3452343444ab3012569ac62b0985a8108e4fcea2063e95a9fe2bea7c47c083</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T12:41:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end--ecd92f33424f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end" /><summary type="html">The longest truce of the war in Ukraine, localised in the region of Kherson, ended on Sunday after Russia refused to extend the ceasefire. The temporary pause in fighting, which began on Tuesday, enabled a humanitarian mission to the Russian-occupied town of Olechky.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Lula's victory, Israeli elections and Spain train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:184202b91db2507138aa803be1e2a0a6f5bd012a4b6b91943ebb633f25b422a4</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T11:14:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash--07ac9159f69c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash" /><summary type="html">From Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's reelection in Brazil's presidential polls, to razor-sharp margins in the Israeli general elections, to a deadly high-speed train collision in Spain, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Youth-led rallies sweep Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82cf48db68af6dc5cba87fc6e5fcf0469ac44423e6cf509005ccd3df2aae7a7a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe--7747234b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe" /><summary type="html">Protests in France have helped inspire youth demonstrations elsewhere in Europe, from Portugal and Italy to Germany. Germany saw particularly large rallies on Saturday, led by a youth initiative whose name roughly translates as “Gen Z has got this”. Demonstrators called for better education and healthcare, stronger climate protection and a more affordable cost of living, while also opposing any return to compulsory military service. However, protests in several major German cities turned violent towards the end of the day, particularly in the financial hub of Frankfurt. Charlotte Hughes reports on the demonstrations across Europe.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria's incumbent Iotova wins presidential runoff vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7995247e345e3f08192d86055a1b3ac75fdd3e97f6b3ac8e0d7ba89a96bd8d</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T05:47:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea--8b2d7985fd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea" /><summary type="html">Bulgarians on Sunday elected incumbent Preisent Iliana Iotova, a proponent of dialogue with Moscow, in a runoff race pitting her against Andrey Gyurov, a former caretaker prime minister backed by the pro-Western opposition. The vote was held as a series of drone attacks in the Black Sea heightened security concerns.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Testimonies from Ukraine's Oleshky: Residents flee Russian-occupied city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e03fd826f3a7f859fe01a4536bea2ab9ead8176f0657096ebe4e0f4336c8c505</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T23:54:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky--738a0891e290.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky" /><summary type="html">In Ukraine, some of the evacuees from the frontline city of Oleshky are beginning to tell their stories. They've been able to leave after four years of Russian occupation. American filmmaker Zarina Zabrisky has lived and reported across the Dnipro River in Ukrainian-controlled Kherson for the past three years. She's been speaking to FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee about the events of the past 24 hours.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'Gen Z' demonstrations across Germany demand more education funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53502b09fbdec79e07ba16f66c7290612a8d20a11046f35e0c5eff8f4579be88</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T20:07:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos--1625df057110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed Saturday in Germany where tens of thousands of young people took to the streets, inspired by similar movements in other European countries. Organized by the "GenZ regelt!" ("Gen Z has got this!") group, marches were held nationwide to demand more funding for education and to protest the high cost of living.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
